            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 86-year-old male admitted on 19/03/2025 with an acute exacerbation of his known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and routine blood tests, confirming an infective exacerbation without evidence of pneumonia or acute heart failure. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), a course of systemic corticosteroids (prednisolone), and supplemental oxygen therapy. He responded well to treatment with improvement in respiratory function. He was discharged on 20/03/2025 in stable condition. Please ensure continuation of his inhaler regimen and arrange early follow-up. Discharge medications and further recommendations are enclosed.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
